                title: 'Lesson 65 - Not a baby',
                passage: "What are you going to do this evening, Jill? I am going to meet some friends, Dad. You must not come home late. You must be home at half past ten. I am eighteen years old, Dad. I am not a baby. Can I have the key to the front door, please? No, you can not. But, Dad! Jill is eighteen years old, Tom. She is not a baby. Give her the key. She always comes home early. Oh, all right! Here you are. But you must not come home after a quarter past eleven. Do you hear? Yes, Dad. Thanks, Mum.",
                passageCn: '今晚你打算干什么，吉尔？我打算去看几个朋友，爸爸。你不准回家太晚。你必须在10点半到家。我已经十八岁了，爸爸。我不是小孩子了。能给我前门钥匙吗？不行，不能给。可是，爸爸！汤姆，吉尔已经十八岁了。她不是小孩子了。把钥匙给她吧。她总是早早回家的。好吧！给你。但你不能超过11点一刻回家。听见了吗？听见了，爸爸。谢谢，妈妈。',
