                title: 'Lesson 143 - A walk through the woods',
                passage: "I live in a very old town which is surrounded by beautiful woods. It is a famous beauty spot. On Sundays, hundreds of people come from the city to see our town and to walk through the woods. Visitors have been asked to keep the woods clean and tidy. Litter baskets have been placed under the trees, but people still throw their rubbish everywhere. Last Wednesday, I went for a walk in the woods. What I saw made me very sad. I counted seven old cars and three old refrigerators. The litter baskets were empty and the ground was covered with pieces of paper, cigarette ends, old tyres, empty bottles and rusty tins. Among the rubbish, I found a sign which said, 'Anyone who leaves litter in these woods will be prosecuted!'",
                passageCn: '我住在一个由美丽树林环绕的古老小镇上。这是一个著名的风景胜地。每逢星期天，有许许多多人从城里来参观我们的小镇并在林中漫步。游客已被要求保持树林的整洁。树下都已放置了垃圾桶，但人们仍然到处乱扔垃圾。上星期三我到树林里去散步。我所见到的一切使我非常难过。我数了数，有7辆旧汽车和3台旧冰箱。垃圾桶是空的，而地上却铺满了纸片、烟头、旧轮胎、空瓶子和生锈的罐头盒。在垃圾堆中我发现了一块牌子，上面写着："凡在此树林里丢弃垃圾者，将依法处置！"',
